----------------------------------------------------------------------

----------------------------------------------------------------------
  DESIGN: Staggered First-Switch Design (SFSD)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  The panel is not CLA, SAD or HAD, but it does satisfy the
  staggered first-switch condition: some groups share the same
  baseline treatment while first switching at different dates.
  First switches occur between t=2004 and t=2004.

  SFSD is the broadest design tested here. Unlike CLA/SAD it
  permits NON-ABSORBING treatment (a group may switch more than
  once, including back to its baseline), and unlike HAD it permits
  HETEROGENEOUS baseline doses.

  Identifying variation: 1 of 1 baseline cell(s) contain
  groups that first switch at different dates.
  Estimator: did_multiplegt_dyn
  See Chapter 8 of the DID textbook.
----------------------------------------------------------------------

. di as text _n "  r(design)    = " as result "`r(design)'"   as text "   expec
> ted HAD"

  r(design)    = SFSD   expected HAD

. di as text    "  r(had_case)  = " as result "`r(had_case)'" as text "   expec
> ted undetermined"
  r(had_case)  =    expected undetermined

. di as text    "  r(n_stayers) = " as result r(n_stayers)
  r(n_stayers) = 2

. di as text    "  r(had_tie)   = " as result r(had_tie)      as text "   expec
> ted 0"
  r(had_tie)   = 0   expected 0

. di as text    "  r(had_d_min) = " as result r(had_d_min)
  r(had_d_min) = 3

. di as text    "  r(qs_stat)   = " as result r(qs_stat)      as text "   expec
> ted missing"
  r(qs_stat)   = .   expected missing

. di as text    "  r(qs_pval)   = " as result r(qs_pval)      as text "   expec
> ted missing"
  r(qs_pval)   = .   expected missing

