----------------------------------------------------------------------
  DESIGN: Heterogeneous Adoption Design (HAD)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  All groups untreated at baseline (t=2001); all 2 treated
  group(s) experience treatment at t=2004, but the size
  of that change varies across groups.

  Sub-case: stayers -- 2 group(s) remain untreated at the switch.
  ATT and WATT are identified under no-anticipation and parallel
  trends, and estimable at the usual sqrt(G) rate.
  Estimator: WATT by ivregress 2sls dY (d = 1(d>0));
             ATT and WATT by did_multiplegt_stat.
  See Chapter 7 of the DID textbook; de Chaisemartin et al. (2026).
----------------------------------------------------------------------

