. whichDIDshouldIuse y g year d, detail

----------------------------------------------------------------------
  whichDIDshouldIuse:  Y=y  G=g  T=year  D=d
  missing treatment: default (less strict)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Panel:    6 periods, calendar 2001 .. 2006
       (t normalized to 1..   6; never-switcher sentinel =    7)
Groups dropped for treatment never observed: 0  (4 -> 4)
Missing treatment (default rules; use , strict to drop instead):
  late entrants, baseline taken at entry:        0
  d missing at start, baseline taken later:      0
  pre-switch gaps read as baseline:              0
  gap right before switch, demoted to control:   0
  controls leaving the panel early:              0
  switchers with d missing after the switch:     0

----------------------------------------------------------------------
  DIAGNOSTICS
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  n_groups             = 4
  n_switchers          = 4
  n_never_treated      = 0   (usable at the earliest switch)
  n_truncated_controls = 0
  never_treated_groups = 0
  any_switchers        = 1
  same_Fg              = 1   (sd(Fg|switchers) = 0)
  switch periods (t)   =  4 ..  4
  switch dates (t_cal) = 2004 .. 2004
  is_binary            = 0   (d in {0, 7})
  is_binary01          = 0
  is_absorbing         = 1
  zero_baseline        = 1   (groups with d_baseline!=0: 0)
  common_baseline      = 1
  heterog_dose         = 1   (sd(first_change) = 2.4494898)
  nonneg_dose          = 1   (min dose at the switch = 2)
  n_stayers            = 0
  had_d_min            = 2   (lowest positive dose at the switch)
  had_tie              = 1
  n_at_d_min           = 2   (groups at the lowest dose)
  n_above_d_min        = 2   (groups above it)
  sfsd_pair            = 0   (groups in cells with a usable pair: 0)
  n_baseline_cells     = 1
  n_sfsd_cells         = 0   (cells carrying timing variation)
  n_post_gap_switchers = 0
----------------------------------------------------------------------

----------------------------------------------------------------------
  DESIGN: Heterogeneous Adoption Design (HAD)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  All groups untreated at baseline (t=2001); all 4 treated
  group(s) experience treatment at t=2004, but the size
  of that change varies across groups.

  Sub-case: no stayers or quasi-stayers -- the lowest dose
  is not close to 0.
    2 groups share the lowest dose (2) and 2 are above it:
    a mass point, not a quasi-stayer. did_had's QS statistic is
    undefined here. If that mass point is genuine -- not an artifact
    of a rounded dose -- the estimand reduces to 2SLS with
    1(d > 2) as instrument. The smaller of the two counts
    above is the binding one: a single group on either side makes
    that instrument weak.
  WARNING: without stayers or quasi-stayers, WATT is not identified
  under parallel trends alone. Using the least-treated as controls
  needs a bounded-heterogeneity assumption (BOUND-HET), which
  pretrends cannot test, and then identifies only the SIGN of WATT.
  Estimator: did_had
  See Chapter 7 of the DID textbook; de Chaisemartin et al. (2026).
----------------------------------------------------------------------

